 <h3 id="relationship-to-graph-coordination">Relationship to graph coordination</h3>
 <p>Graph-theoretic traversal concerns vertices, edges and legal abstract transitions. The rotor-router literature studies such discrete models [R1]. The physical execution layer adds evidence for an assigned geographical obligation; it does not change rotor order, implement gossip or prove an arbitrary planner correct after reassignment. <strong>No rotor-router or gossip algorithm was implemented or run in this campaign.</strong> Algorithm independence is demonstrated by the API boundary, not by a multi-planner experimental comparison.</p>
+<p>The intended future dependency is <strong>external graph decision → SDK edge request → onboard VECR execution and evidence → attempt result → external graph-state decision</strong>. A rotor-router application would own edge selection and rotor state. SwarmKit would own physical execution, evidence qualification and bounded recovery. The application adapter must explicitly handle pending, interrupted and unknown attempts; a command ACK cannot count as completed physical work.</p>
